1
00:00:01,075 --> 00:00:02,982
Sync and corrections by n17t01
www.addic7ed.com

2
00:00:05,439 --> 00:00:06,732
<i>Raising kids--</i>

3
00:00:06,972 --> 00:00:09,778
<i>it seems to go by</i>
<i>in the blink of an eye.</i>

4
00:00:10,059 --> 00:00:12,952
<i>But it's all worth it</i>
<i>'cause you know someday</i>

5
00:00:13,046 --> 00:00:14,802
<i>they're gonna grow up and be...</i>

6
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:16,725
Why are you lurking
outside my door?

7
00:00:16,817 --> 00:00:18,744
God, it's like you're stalking me!

8
00:00:19,404 --> 00:00:20,812
<i>Awful.</i>

9
00:00:22,424 --> 00:00:24,687
Ugh. Is it me,
or is Axl being a bigger jerk

10
00:00:24,823 --> 00:00:26,331
than usual lately?

11
00:00:26,455 --> 00:00:27,628
I don't know.

12
00:00:27,712 --> 00:00:30,132
Seems like about the normal
amount of jerk to me.

13
00:00:30,219 --> 00:00:33,043
No, I'm serious, Mike.
He's been horrible to me.

14
00:00:33,176 --> 00:00:34,749
I'm just trying to get
some answers out of him

15
00:00:34,844 --> 00:00:37,259
about his graduation party,
and he's all, like...

16
00:00:37,348 --> 00:00:38,295
"What's with you?

17
00:00:38,391 --> 00:00:40,301
"Stop stalking me.
If it bugs you so much,

18
00:00:40,386 --> 00:00:41,598
why don't <i>you</i> flush it?"

19
00:00:41,705 --> 00:00:43,921
I don't know how much more
I can take.

20
00:00:44,023 --> 00:00:46,876
And look around this place. I got a high
tolerance for pain.

21
00:00:48,284 --> 00:00:49,553
Hmm. Hey, Brick,

22
00:00:49,664 --> 00:00:50,644
I got a notice from the school.

23
00:00:50,734 --> 00:00:52,312
You gotta collect all your stuff
from the Lost and Found

24
00:00:52,412 --> 00:00:53,235
by the end of the week,

25
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:54,800
or they're gonna donate it
to the poor.

26
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:57,407
Get my stuff, Brick.
I want my stuff back.

27
00:00:57,494 --> 00:00:59,179
Hmm. I don't recall
losing anything.

28
00:00:59,258 --> 00:01:00,693
What kind of stuff
are we talking about?

29
00:01:00,767 --> 00:01:02,985
Huh. A lunch box,
an IU sweatshirt,

30
00:01:03,106 --> 00:01:06,002
a winter jacket, a rain jacket,
the Donahues' jacket,

31
00:01:06,152 --> 00:01:07,873
the good flashlight,
the bad flashlight,

32
00:01:07,958 --> 00:01:10,090
a bubble umbrella,
and I'm gonna be conservative

33
00:01:10,183 --> 00:01:12,447
and say, oh,
20 pairs of mittens.

34
00:01:12,544 --> 00:01:13,114
Huh.

35
00:01:13,222 --> 00:01:14,331
Since you know exactly
what's missing,

36
00:01:14,422 --> 00:01:17,516
maybe <i>you</i> should go. You really
seem to have a handle on this.

37
00:01:19,225 --> 00:01:20,567
Excuse me, everyone.

38
00:01:20,937 --> 00:01:23,967
As you know, I'm taking
my driver's exam on Friday,

39
00:01:24,082 --> 00:01:26,622
and since the sixth time
is the charm,

40
00:01:26,751 --> 00:01:29,044
I would like to make our last
week on the bus together

41
00:01:29,146 --> 00:01:32,442
a week to remember,
and I would like to kick it off

42
00:01:32,557 --> 00:01:36,751
by having my bus buddies,
AKA you guys,

43
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:39,266
sign my yearbook. Yeah?

44
00:01:39,358 --> 00:01:41,008
<i>Yep, it was the end of an era,</i>

45
00:01:41,159 --> 00:01:43,653
<i>'cause for Sue,</i>
<i>the bus wasn't just the bus.</i>

46
00:01:43,775 --> 00:01:47,170
<i>It was a rolling</i>
<i>yellow memory making machine.</i>

47
00:01:47,912 --> 00:01:50,619
Thanks, guys.
I'm really gonna cherish this.

48
00:01:52,602 --> 00:01:55,683
Ha ha. Very funny, guys.

49
00:01:55,792 --> 00:01:59,521
I hope not having lunch today
was worth that prank.

50
00:02:03,250 --> 00:02:06,067
Looks like
somebody really struck it rich

51
00:02:06,155 --> 00:02:07,790
at the Lost and Found.

52
00:02:07,962 --> 00:02:11,906
You're Brick Heck, right?
You're the class historian.

53
00:02:12,233 --> 00:02:14,047
- Am I?
<i>- He was.</i>

54
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:17,023
So... how is your slide show
coming along?

55
00:02:17,125 --> 00:02:20,579
Since I'm the vice principal,
that's kind of my baby.

56
00:02:20,670 --> 00:02:21,599
Slide show?

57
00:02:21,690 --> 00:02:23,982
Well, you know,
for the final assembly,

58
00:02:24,062 --> 00:02:27,635
when the historian presents
his big presentation.

59
00:02:27,725 --> 00:02:29,641
Why do you think you've been
taking all those pictures

60
00:02:29,748 --> 00:02:31,720
for the past four years?

61
00:02:31,910 --> 00:02:34,565
For the assembly, of course.

62
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:36,608
That's exactly why I've been
taking all those pictures,

63
00:02:36,732 --> 00:02:39,085
which I definitely did do,
by the way.

64
00:02:39,167 --> 00:02:41,135
Now remember, dear,
your photo montage

65
00:02:41,251 --> 00:02:43,637
should be poignant
and heartfelt.

66
00:02:43,783 --> 00:02:45,337
We've allotted 15 minutes,

67
00:02:45,434 --> 00:02:48,349
but you can go a full 20
if you need to.

68
00:02:48,483 --> 00:02:50,957
Oh, good. That takes
some of the pressure off.

69
00:02:51,079 --> 00:02:53,626
Really looking forward to it.

70
00:03:00,189 --> 00:03:02,191
Oh, good, you're home.
I...

71
00:03:02,310 --> 00:03:03,679
I need you to give me
some answers

72
00:03:03,816 --> 00:03:05,533
about your graduation party.

73
00:03:05,637 --> 00:03:07,081
Oh, you still talking
about that?

74
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:10,122
Yes, I am, because you won't.

75
00:03:10,261 --> 00:03:13,106
So how many of your
friends do you think will be coming?

76
00:03:13,311 --> 00:03:15,107
Unknown.

77
00:03:15,507 --> 00:03:18,150
- Will Sean and Darrin wanna
bring their parents? - Unknown.

78
00:03:18,297 --> 00:03:19,502
What about food and drinks?

79
00:03:19,604 --> 00:03:21,031
"Un" and "known."

80
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,495
Well, <i>can</i> it be known?

81
00:03:22,642 --> 00:03:25,314
Can you give me maybe
one second of your attention

82
00:03:25,449 --> 00:03:27,089
so that I can know
some of this stuff?

83
00:03:27,204 --> 00:03:29,493
Look, your graduation
is a big deal, Axl.

84
00:03:29,612 --> 00:03:31,147
It wasn't exactly breezy
getting you

85
00:03:31,237 --> 00:03:32,566
through four years
of high school,

86
00:03:32,683 --> 00:03:34,619
and we would like
to celebrate it.

87
00:03:34,718 --> 00:03:36,020
Fine.
Whatever you want.

88
00:03:36,121 --> 00:03:38,977
No, it's not whatever <i>I</i> want.
It's whatever <i>you</i> want.

89
00:03:39,113 --> 00:03:42,025
Ho ho ho! That's hilarious.
This is not what I <i>want.</i>

90
00:03:42,137 --> 00:03:43,408
I just wanna hang out
with my friends.

91
00:03:43,499 --> 00:03:44,810
I don't even <i>want</i> a party.

92
00:03:44,916 --> 00:03:47,142
You wanna give me what I want?
How about a car?

93
00:03:51,232 --> 00:03:53,056
Oh, my God.
She's here again.

94
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:54,890
Don't shut the door in my face,

95
00:03:54,999 --> 00:03:56,231
and don't call me "she."

96
00:03:56,301 --> 00:03:57,640
You're female, are you not?

97
00:03:57,730 --> 00:03:59,751
What am I supposed
to call you? God!

98
00:04:00,539 --> 00:04:01,822
We are not finished here, Axl.

99
00:04:01,919 --> 00:04:03,692
I literally need just
two minutes of your time.

100
00:04:03,777 --> 00:04:04,959
I don't think
that's too much to ask.

101
00:04:05,058 --> 00:04:06,970
Actually, it is. I'm already late
for Darrin's party.

102
00:04:07,065 --> 00:04:07,850
And I wanna get there

103
00:04:07,935 --> 00:04:10,525
before all the jell-o sh... alad is gone.

104
00:04:10,628 --> 00:04:13,045
Look, I'll be home by 11:30.
We can talk about it then.

105
00:04:13,166 --> 00:04:15,569
Fine. I will be waiting
for you right here

106
00:04:15,671 --> 00:04:18,510
- at exactly 11:30, and I
expect you to be here. - I will.

107
00:04:18,618 --> 00:04:19,647
With your full attention.

108
00:04:19,763 --> 00:04:20,639
My full attention.

109
00:04:20,742 --> 00:04:22,238
And no jell-o
on your breath.

110
00:04:22,345 --> 00:04:24,088
11:30. I want you
to give me your word.

111
00:04:24,195 --> 00:04:25,421
Fine. You have my word.

112
00:04:31,125 --> 00:04:32,084
<i>I'm just gonna say it</i>

113
00:04:32,184 --> 00:04:33,702
<i>'cause it might help others</i>
<i>in the future.</i>

114
00:04:33,824 --> 00:04:36,666
<i>A teenager's
word doesn't mean squat.</i>

115
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:39,387
<i>It was midnight,</i>
<i>and still no sign of Axl.</i>

116
00:04:40,711 --> 00:04:41,991
Hey, mom, quick thing.

117
00:04:42,101 --> 00:04:44,885
I need you to take about
200 pictures of my classmates

118
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:46,623
and set them to music
in a slide show.

119
00:04:46,750 --> 00:04:49,154
It should be touching
but not schmaltzy,

120
00:04:49,286 --> 00:04:50,998
funny, but without
trying too hard.

121
00:04:51,101 --> 00:04:54,029
And if you could have it ready
Friday morning by 10:00,

122
00:04:54,127 --> 00:04:56,554
that'd be great.
11:00 at the latest. Night.

123
00:04:56,651 --> 00:04:58,147
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Brick.

124
00:04:58,269 --> 00:04:59,706
How long have you known
about this?

125
00:04:59,793 --> 00:05:01,275
What's today? Thursday?

126
00:05:01,369 --> 00:05:03,550
About... four years.

127
00:05:03,655 --> 00:05:05,170
- Brick!
- It's not my fault.

128
00:05:05,261 --> 00:05:06,661
They should have voted
for Jay Gold.

129
00:05:06,782 --> 00:05:08,525
I got elected based
on one good speech

130
00:05:08,635 --> 00:05:10,230
and didn't have the skills
to back it up.

131
00:05:10,333 --> 00:05:11,735
It's really what's wrong
with politics.

132
00:05:11,831 --> 00:05:13,235
I'm sorry, Brick,
but you're gonna have to

133
00:05:13,334 --> 00:05:15,569
figure this one out on your own,
'cause I'm over it.

134
00:05:15,654 --> 00:05:17,958
I'm done getting in the middle
of my kids' lives.

135
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:20,609
Hey, where are you going?

136
00:05:21,154 --> 00:05:22,457
Unknown.

137
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:34,843
53 times without stopping.

138
00:05:34,909 --> 00:05:36,788
What, you don't believe me?
Hmm? I'll do it right now.

139
00:05:36,869 --> 00:05:37,964
Someone give me two straws.

140
00:05:38,083 --> 00:05:41,088
I'm telling you.

141
00:05:44,602 --> 00:05:46,069
<i>Dude.</i>

142
00:05:54,988 --> 00:05:56,510
Somebody in our family
better be dead right now,

143
00:05:56,610 --> 00:05:58,427
and not some weird cousin
I've never met.

144
00:05:58,512 --> 00:05:59,786
I'm talking dad, Brick, or Sue.

145
00:05:59,878 --> 00:06:02,804
Nobody's dead, but if you
don't get in my car right now,

146
00:06:02,914 --> 00:06:04,155
it can be arranged.

147
00:06:04,247 --> 00:06:06,943
Just go, please, and I'll meet
you outside in three minutes.

148
00:06:07,018 --> 00:06:08,075
- I promise.
- Yeah.

149
00:06:08,194 --> 00:06:09,742
You already promised
to be home by 11:30,

150
00:06:09,835 --> 00:06:12,663
so I think the promise ship
has sailed. Hi, Sean.

151
00:06:12,752 --> 00:06:13,880
Oh!

152
00:06:15,874 --> 00:06:18,182
You don't wanna do this, mom,
seriously.

153
00:06:18,296 --> 00:06:20,133
This is the most embarrassing
thing any parent

154
00:06:20,245 --> 00:06:22,026
has ever done, ever.

155
00:06:22,316 --> 00:06:23,653
You sure about that?

156
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:28,203
Ooh. I like this song.

157
00:06:28,506 --> 00:06:29,689
What are you doing?

158
00:06:29,801 --> 00:06:32,901
I don't know. This groove
kinda makes me feel like...

159
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,257
gettin' down.

160
00:06:34,354 --> 00:06:35,888
Mom, no.
Don't do this to me.

161
00:06:35,986 --> 00:06:37,886
This is my last high school
party. I can't end like this.

162
00:06:37,989 --> 00:06:39,428
Darrin!

163
00:06:39,619 --> 00:06:41,017
No! No!

164
00:06:48,204 --> 00:06:50,270
You are the worst mother ever!

165
00:06:50,371 --> 00:06:51,966
Oh, tell me something
I don't know.

166
00:06:52,087 --> 00:06:55,039
Do you know how many years
of cool you just erased

167
00:06:55,146 --> 00:06:56,782
with your stupid
mama pajama dance?

168
00:06:56,874 --> 00:06:59,114
Hey, I thought very hard
before I pulled that rip cord,

169
00:06:59,204 --> 00:07:00,839
but it's the only weapon
I have left.

170
00:07:00,928 --> 00:07:03,271
You know, you have been
impossible lately.

171
00:07:03,362 --> 00:07:05,263
Maybe you should stop trying
to boss me around all the time

172
00:07:05,374 --> 00:07:07,785
and talk to me like a person.

173
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:10,871
What?! All I've been
trying to do is talk to you,

174
00:07:10,977 --> 00:07:12,262
and you just keep running away.

175
00:07:12,379 --> 00:07:15,681
You gave me your word that
you would be home <i>an hour ago.</i>

176
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:17,683
"I'm Axl. I just give
people my word

177
00:07:17,788 --> 00:07:19,462
without even thinking
about what it means."

178
00:07:19,556 --> 00:07:21,241
Oh, we're doing
impressions now? Hmm?

179
00:07:21,331 --> 00:07:23,664
Okay. "I'm mom.
Uh, I never stop talking,

180
00:07:23,762 --> 00:07:25,932
and I'm in your face
24 hours a day."

181
00:07:26,048 --> 00:07:27,983
All right, that's it.
I'm sick of your attitude!

182
00:07:28,071 --> 00:07:29,747
- Get out of my sight!
- Fine!

183
00:07:29,842 --> 00:07:31,506
Don't you walk away from me!

184
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:33,848
Oh, my God! She's nuts.
She's totally nuts!

185
00:07:33,945 --> 00:07:35,603
I told you
not to call me "she."

186
00:07:35,692 --> 00:07:36,929
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Break it up.

187
00:07:37,002 --> 00:07:38,453
You, in your room.
You, in the kitchen.

188
00:07:38,543 --> 00:07:39,682
Whoa, hey.
This is not my fault.

189
00:07:39,763 --> 00:07:41,472
Mom's freaking out on me
for no reason.

190
00:07:41,655 --> 00:07:43,175
I'm freaking out
for a very good reason.

191
00:07:43,273 --> 00:07:45,385
He is making me freak out,
and I'm not freaking out.

192
00:07:45,511 --> 00:07:46,781
Look, I don't know
what's going on here,

193
00:07:46,875 --> 00:07:48,741
but I know I gotta side
with her, so go.

194
00:07:48,842 --> 00:07:50,939
Hey. Wha-- uh... ugh!

195
00:07:52,085 --> 00:07:54,496
I am going to
kill him, I tell you!

196
00:07:54,588 --> 00:07:55,497
I'm gonna kill him.

197
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:57,279
Just relax. He's not
gonna be here much longer.

198
00:07:57,359 --> 00:07:58,835
Then I'll have to act fast,
won't I?

199
00:07:58,949 --> 00:08:02,446
I can't <i>stand</i> him, Mike.
I just hate his stupid face.

200
00:08:02,556 --> 00:08:03,967
I swear to God,
when he goes off to college,

201
00:08:04,069 --> 00:08:05,112
I'm not even gonna miss him.

202
00:08:05,213 --> 00:08:07,684
Look, all this
fighting is just nature's way

203
00:08:07,816 --> 00:08:10,202
of helping you guys deal
with the fact he's leaving.

204
00:08:10,302 --> 00:08:11,954
You think mama birds push
their babies out of the nest

205
00:08:12,046 --> 00:08:14,527
to help 'em fly?
Maybe they're just sick of 'em.

206
00:08:14,772 --> 00:08:17,014
Trust me, Frankie. It's
the natural order of things.

207
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:18,503
It's why you guys
have been annoying each other

208
00:08:18,594 --> 00:08:19,585
so much lately.

209
00:08:19,691 --> 00:08:22,785
- I'm not doing anything.
I'm being great. It's him. - Uh-huh.

210
00:08:22,881 --> 00:08:24,710
Are you in your pajamas
with your coat on?

211
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:29,003
I was cold, and I thought
we were hating him right now.

212
00:08:29,169 --> 00:08:32,178
He... is a bad, bad child,

213
00:08:32,290 --> 00:08:34,619
and <i>you</i> are a wonderful mother.

214
00:08:34,958 --> 00:08:36,145
Thank you.

215
00:08:37,787 --> 00:08:39,745
I would just like
to remind everyone

216
00:08:39,843 --> 00:08:42,938
that today is going to be
our final ride together,

217
00:08:43,143 --> 00:08:46,777
and to thank you guys
for all the good times we had,

218
00:08:46,958 --> 00:08:48,808
I baked some
peanut butter cookies

219
00:08:48,909 --> 00:08:50,485
'cause I know
someone on this bus

220
00:08:50,594 --> 00:08:52,673
really likes peanut butter.

221
00:08:52,763 --> 00:08:53,999
Ha ha.

222
00:08:54,277 --> 00:08:57,988
<i>And</i> if <i>you</i> guys would like
to thank <i>me</i>

223
00:08:58,102 --> 00:09:01,268
with a round of
"For She's A Jolly Good Fellow,"

224
00:09:01,421 --> 00:09:04,226
let's just say
I would not hate that.

225
00:09:05,381 --> 00:09:07,654
Why don't I just get it started?

226
00:09:08,114 --> 00:09:11,488
♪ For she's
a jolly good fellow ♪

227
00:09:11,633 --> 00:09:14,202
♪ for she's a... jolly... ♪

228
00:09:15,977 --> 00:09:22,503
You know, I have tried and tried
with you guys all year.

229
00:09:22,593 --> 00:09:25,235
But you guys have no bus spirit.

230
00:09:25,342 --> 00:09:29,154
And you know what?
I <i>am</i> a jolly good fellow.

231
00:09:29,297 --> 00:09:32,803
<i>You guys</i> aren't.
You're bad fellows!

232
00:09:33,791 --> 00:09:35,199
Yes, Brian?

233
00:09:35,372 --> 00:09:38,123
I think I speak for all of us
when I say

234
00:09:38,353 --> 00:09:40,570
please pass that test.

235
00:09:40,681 --> 00:09:42,167
Past that test!

236
00:09:42,289 --> 00:09:43,886
Pass that test!

237
00:09:43,978 --> 00:09:47,086
Pass that test! Pass that test!

238
00:09:47,406 --> 00:09:52,210
Pass that test! Pass that test!
Pass that test!

239
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,041
Ahem.

240
00:09:58,767 --> 00:10:00,758
Hi there, Brick.

241
00:10:00,886 --> 00:10:03,816
How's my favorite
class historian doing?

242
00:10:03,936 --> 00:10:06,206
Actually, there's been
a little hiccup

243
00:10:06,365 --> 00:10:08,658
with the photo montage,
but the good news is,

244
00:10:08,746 --> 00:10:11,242
you'll have an extra 15 minutes
to play with at the assembly.

245
00:10:11,356 --> 00:10:13,739
Oh, well, these things happen.

246
00:10:13,834 --> 00:10:15,030
Oh, I knew you'd understand.

247
00:10:15,242 --> 00:10:17,868
But they don't happen to me.
Now you listen to me.

248
00:10:18,028 --> 00:10:19,785
And you listen good,
you little punk.

249
00:10:19,967 --> 00:10:23,423
You're gonna do the job you were
elected to do four years ago,

250
00:10:23,537 --> 00:10:27,949
or I will turn you inside out
and wear you like a hat.

251
00:10:28,071 --> 00:10:30,994
Ha. I know everyone thinks
the vice principal's a joke.

252
00:10:31,830 --> 00:10:33,414
I hear the whispers.

253
00:10:33,521 --> 00:10:36,082
I don't like it when people
whisper about me, Brick.

254
00:10:36,212 --> 00:10:37,307
Got it?

255
00:10:37,661 --> 00:10:39,253
Got it.
Got it.

256
00:10:39,373 --> 00:10:40,863
Sorry!
Sorry.

257
00:10:40,978 --> 00:10:42,203
I can't stop whispering!

258
00:10:42,297 --> 00:10:46,451
- Whispering.
- This photo montage is the only thing

259
00:10:46,551 --> 00:10:49,533
the Principal doesn't have
her stinkin' paws all over,

260
00:10:49,697 --> 00:10:51,122
and if you mess it up,

261
00:10:51,263 --> 00:10:54,379
I will make your life
a living hell.

262
00:10:54,497 --> 00:10:57,084
I have connections
in middle school,

263
00:10:57,234 --> 00:11:00,167
and I can make sure you get
the smelliest locker

264
00:11:00,298 --> 00:11:01,487
and the meanest teachers

265
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:05,133
and <i>extra gym.</i>

266
00:11:05,242 --> 00:11:06,126
Oh, no.

267
00:11:06,224 --> 00:11:07,406
Oh, yes.

268
00:11:07,530 --> 00:11:09,464
Well, anyway,

269
00:11:09,563 --> 00:11:12,354
I can't wait to see
your presentation, dear.

270
00:11:21,916 --> 00:11:24,394
Now remember, Sue,
this is just like a car,

271
00:11:24,517 --> 00:11:26,567
only much bigger
and harder to drive.

272
00:11:26,665 --> 00:11:28,763
Why did Axl have
to take your car?

273
00:11:28,932 --> 00:11:30,420
What if I fail again?

274
00:11:30,604 --> 00:11:32,826
I cannot get back
on that bus, dad.

275
00:11:32,972 --> 00:11:34,255
Sue, listen to me.

276
00:11:34,481 --> 00:11:37,903
You have screwed up
this driving test so many ways,

277
00:11:38,004 --> 00:11:41,133
I can't think of another mistake
you could possibly make.

278
00:11:41,759 --> 00:11:44,636
Aw! Thanks for the pep talk,
dad.

279
00:11:44,784 --> 00:11:47,353
Okay. Let's do this!

280
00:11:47,452 --> 00:11:49,451
Whoo!

281
00:11:53,907 --> 00:11:55,325
Sue Heck.

282
00:12:03,324 --> 00:12:05,138
And now with no further ado,

283
00:12:05,256 --> 00:12:08,559
your class historian,
Brick Heck,

284
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:11,059
will take you
on a magical, musical journey

285
00:12:11,170 --> 00:12:14,735
of your years
at Orson Elementary.

286
00:12:14,844 --> 00:12:16,127
Brick?

287
00:12:16,373 --> 00:12:20,431
You better
blow the doors off this place.

288
00:12:27,247 --> 00:12:28,821
Memories.

289
00:12:30,439 --> 00:12:31,550
I could show you all

290
00:12:31,669 --> 00:12:34,083
pictures of your time here
at Orson Elementary,

291
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:37,401
but those would be <i>my</i> memories,
not yours.

292
00:12:37,678 --> 00:12:41,407
So instead, I invite you
to close your eyes

293
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:43,360
and picture your own memories.

294
00:12:46,694 --> 00:12:48,913
Remember the field trip
to the Indiana Dunes

295
00:12:49,024 --> 00:12:50,078
in second grade?

296
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:51,930
I don't, but maybe you do.

297
00:12:52,037 --> 00:12:53,572
Maybe you had a great time.

298
00:12:55,851 --> 00:12:57,985
What about the time that you

299
00:12:58,072 --> 00:12:59,491
and your friend
and your other friend

300
00:12:59,590 --> 00:13:01,376
locked arms on the playground?

301
00:13:01,479 --> 00:13:03,242
Boy, you guys are close.

302
00:13:04,637 --> 00:13:07,873
And now sit back and enjoy
a musical montage

303
00:13:07,978 --> 00:13:10,840
of all your best memories,
artfully put together

304
00:13:10,957 --> 00:13:13,334
in your own imagination,
while I hum the tune

305
00:13:13,437 --> 00:13:15,487
to the appropriate,
if not overused,

306
00:13:15,593 --> 00:13:19,158
graduation anthem,
"We Are Young" by Fun.

307
00:13:27,579 --> 00:13:28,812
Who <i>is</i> that?

308
00:13:28,914 --> 00:13:30,374
Did we vote for him?

309
00:13:30,503 --> 00:13:32,181
He's weird.

310
00:13:32,509 --> 00:13:37,086
<i>So Brick left elementary school</i>
<i>with his reputation intact.</i>

311
00:13:41,733 --> 00:13:43,484
- Nailed it.
- This isn't over.

312
00:13:43,587 --> 00:13:46,504
I will hunt you like a dog
in the street.

313
00:13:47,081 --> 00:13:49,550
Well, wasn't that delightful?

314
00:13:49,682 --> 00:13:53,911
And now Mimi Millhauser
on the flutophone.

315
00:13:54,118 --> 00:13:56,586
Okay, Sue, in about a half mile,
you're gonna wanna take--

316
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:58,537
I know. Take a right
at the stop sign,

317
00:13:58,669 --> 00:14:00,878
a left by the yellow house
with the apple tree in the yard,

318
00:14:01,025 --> 00:14:03,634
then bring it down
to 25 miles an hour

319
00:14:03,734 --> 00:14:05,140
for the school zone.

320
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:07,599
This is not my first barbecue.

321
00:14:08,678 --> 00:14:10,852
Nice signal.

322
00:14:13,547 --> 00:14:16,356
And... nice turn.

323
00:14:16,465 --> 00:14:19,338
<i>Only six blocks to go,</i>
<i>and Sue was doing great.</i>

324
00:14:19,482 --> 00:14:21,855
<i>Maybe it was all</i>
<i>her experience paying off.</i>

325
00:14:21,938 --> 00:14:23,728
<i>Maybe it was bobblehead Jesus.</i>

326
00:14:23,816 --> 00:14:25,801
<i>But of course, Sue being Sue...</i>

327
00:14:27,677 --> 00:14:28,690
Windshield obstructed.

328
00:14:28,778 --> 00:14:29,933
Activating wipers.

329
00:14:30,634 --> 00:14:32,275
Peripheral vision compromised.

330
00:14:32,558 --> 00:14:33,854
I really think we should stop.

331
00:14:33,950 --> 00:14:35,215
Don't worry. I got this.

332
00:14:36,601 --> 00:14:37,433
Whoa-oh.

333
00:14:38,844 --> 00:14:41,441
- Watch out!
- No choice but to go through!

334
00:14:44,930 --> 00:14:46,298
Oh, God.

335
00:14:46,384 --> 00:14:48,311
Mattress! Oh!

336
00:14:48,364 --> 00:14:49,616
It's okay!
I can still see!

337
00:14:49,678 --> 00:14:53,107
For the love of God, pull over!
I have children!

338
00:14:53,208 --> 00:14:56,501
No! I only have
two blocks left!

339
00:14:56,603 --> 00:14:58,147
Pothole.

340
00:14:58,280 --> 00:14:59,738
Not a problem!

341
00:15:03,087 --> 00:15:04,409
Page 47 in the manual--

342
00:15:04,538 --> 00:15:07,020
how to stay calm
in a hazardous situation!

343
00:15:17,032 --> 00:15:19,635
I've been doing this for 30 years.

344
00:15:20,181 --> 00:15:22,783
And that was the single
greatest piece of driving

345
00:15:22,899 --> 00:15:24,574
I have ever seen.

346
00:15:24,690 --> 00:15:27,601
Congratulations, Sue Heck.
You passed.

347
00:15:27,721 --> 00:15:32,204
Aah!

348
00:15:40,595 --> 00:15:43,237
Axl, come on! Let's go!
I wanna get a good seat.

349
00:15:43,345 --> 00:15:44,837
I'm coming. God!

350
00:15:44,928 --> 00:15:46,126
Did I mention
that the examiner said

351
00:15:46,239 --> 00:15:49,595
it was the single greatest
piece of driving he's ever seen?

352
00:15:49,691 --> 00:15:51,178
- I'm sure you did great, honey.
- Yeah.

353
00:15:51,288 --> 00:15:53,220
She did do great.
Sue, you're an excellent driver.

354
00:15:53,347 --> 00:15:55,205
Can I drive the family
to graduation?

355
00:15:55,349 --> 00:15:57,008
Absolutely not.

356
00:15:59,473 --> 00:16:01,149
No, no, no, no, no. Unh-unh.

357
00:16:01,335 --> 00:16:04,185
- What? - You're not wearing
white socks with dress pants.

358
00:16:04,292 --> 00:16:05,534
Go change.

359
00:16:05,635 --> 00:16:06,417
Why?

360
00:16:06,538 --> 00:16:08,671
Because you're gonna be onstage,
and everybody'll see 'em,

361
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:09,775
and it looks ridiculous.

362
00:16:09,874 --> 00:16:12,613
Nobody's gonna be looking
at my socks. Let's just go!

363
00:16:12,728 --> 00:16:14,050
Come on. Brick's waiting
in the car. Let's go.

364
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:16,698
Axl, I am serious.
Go put on some black socks.

365
00:16:16,792 --> 00:16:18,838
Why do you even care about this?
They're my feet.

366
00:16:18,976 --> 00:16:20,654
The doctor pulled you out of me
with those feet,

367
00:16:20,741 --> 00:16:22,065
so I think I have some say.

368
00:16:22,218 --> 00:16:24,852
Look...
now put these <i>on.</i>

369
00:16:25,062 --> 00:16:26,283
Make me.

370
00:16:27,699 --> 00:16:30,144
You are not leaving this house.
Don't you dare leave this house!

371
00:16:30,293 --> 00:16:31,750
Oh, my God.
What are you doing?

372
00:16:31,828 --> 00:16:34,432
Change... your... socks!

373
00:16:34,517 --> 00:16:35,740
Oh!

374
00:16:35,917 --> 00:16:37,439
All right, if you're not
gonna change 'em, I will.

375
00:16:37,534 --> 00:16:39,164
- Hey! You can't do this! - Give me that.
Take your-- get your shoes off.

376
00:16:39,286 --> 00:16:41,539
- Get your shoe off.
- Aah! No.

377
00:16:41,634 --> 00:16:42,732
I'm telling you,
you're changing those socks!

378
00:16:42,812 --> 00:16:43,860
No! Never!

379
00:16:43,968 --> 00:16:45,723
- Never!
- Get back here.

380
00:16:45,822 --> 00:16:46,663
Ohh!

381
00:16:48,705 --> 00:16:50,768
- Aah!
- Uhh!

382
00:16:50,879 --> 00:16:54,354
You are not going anywhere
in those socks!

383
00:16:54,471 --> 00:16:56,381
Aah! You're hurting me!
You're hurting your son!

384
00:16:56,507 --> 00:16:57,745
We are civilized people.

385
00:16:57,880 --> 00:17:00,173
There are rules to society,

386
00:17:00,271 --> 00:17:01,637
and you're gonna learn 'em,
damn it!

387
00:17:01,726 --> 00:17:04,121
She's crazy!
Your wife is crazy!

388
00:17:04,298 --> 00:17:07,207
Should've put a fence around
this place a long time ago.

389
00:17:12,229 --> 00:17:13,488
No!

390
00:17:13,984 --> 00:17:15,355
Where do you think
you're goin'?

391
00:17:15,442 --> 00:17:17,277
I'm getting a ride
to graduation with the Donahues!

392
00:17:17,388 --> 00:17:20,170
Fine!
Maybe we won't even go!

393
00:17:20,356 --> 00:17:21,788
So we're not going?

394
00:17:21,892 --> 00:17:25,093
Oh, we're goin'. I need to
make sure he's really leaving.

395
00:17:33,287 --> 00:17:35,066
As we say
good-bye to high school,

396
00:17:35,169 --> 00:17:37,186
we look ahead
to the next chapter of our lives

397
00:17:37,305 --> 00:17:39,051
and the adventures
it will bring--

398
00:17:39,186 --> 00:17:41,824
college, jobs, travel...

399
00:17:41,928 --> 00:17:44,004
Hey, that guy's wearing
white socks just like Axl's.

400
00:17:45,141 --> 00:17:49,409
Matter of fact, a lot of people
are wearing white socks.

401
00:17:49,557 --> 00:17:51,972
White socks, white socks,
flip-flops.

402
00:17:52,062 --> 00:17:52,940
We get it, Brick.

403
00:17:53,035 --> 00:17:55,031
So in closing, I just wanna say

404
00:17:55,167 --> 00:17:57,783
even though
I'm a pretty cynical person,

405
00:17:57,957 --> 00:18:00,138
I'm really gonna miss
this place.

406
00:18:01,001 --> 00:18:02,907
As Shel Silverstein wrote,

407
00:18:03,073 --> 00:18:07,111
"There <i>are</i> no happy endings.
Endings are the saddest part.

408
00:18:07,294 --> 00:18:12,307
So just give me a happy middle
and a very happy start."

409
00:18:12,425 --> 00:18:13,904
And thanks to all of you

410
00:18:14,031 --> 00:18:17,044
for giving me
a very happy start here.

411
00:18:17,175 --> 00:18:18,299
Whoo!

412
00:18:27,233 --> 00:18:29,293
Thomas Halverson.

413
00:18:29,449 --> 00:18:30,540
Yeah.

414
00:18:30,643 --> 00:18:32,588
- Whoo.
- That was a squeaker, wasn't it?

415
00:18:32,977 --> 00:18:35,896
Yeah. Julie Harris. Yeah.

416
00:18:36,146 --> 00:18:38,637
Good luck with the baby.
Last one.

417
00:18:38,737 --> 00:18:40,196
Robert Hatfield.

418
00:18:40,311 --> 00:18:43,060
All right. You behave tonight,
Robert. You behave.

419
00:18:43,227 --> 00:18:44,543
Elizabeth Hayworth.

420
00:18:44,715 --> 00:18:46,571
Here you go.

421
00:18:46,790 --> 00:18:48,148
<i>As I watched my first son</i>

422
00:18:48,238 --> 00:18:49,932
<i>about to become</i>
<i>a high school graduate,</i>

423
00:18:50,089 --> 00:18:52,037
<i>I realized that Mike was right.</i>

424
00:18:52,167 --> 00:18:53,798
<i>There is a natural order</i>
<i>to things,</i>

425
00:18:53,918 --> 00:18:56,588
<i>and by the time they go, you're ready.</i>

426
00:18:56,683 --> 00:18:59,285
- Axl Heck.
- Whoo!

427
00:19:04,875 --> 00:19:06,464
I'm not ready!

428
00:19:08,064 --> 00:19:10,870
- Brian Hedberg.
- Oh, no.

429
00:19:11,495 --> 00:19:12,811
Good luck at computer school.

430
00:19:12,944 --> 00:19:15,209
I'm not ready!

431
00:19:17,259 --> 00:19:18,628
Mark Hef--

432
00:19:21,378 --> 00:19:22,877
Mark Hefferman.

433
00:19:23,851 --> 00:19:25,258
Jessica--

434
00:19:31,006 --> 00:19:32,465
Sarah Humphreys.

435
00:19:43,467 --> 00:19:45,301
Well, you said
it was impossible

436
00:19:45,412 --> 00:19:47,074
for me to miss 32 days
of senior year

437
00:19:47,167 --> 00:19:48,249
and still graduate.

438
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:50,828
Now who seems like the idiot?
Huh?

439
00:19:51,013 --> 00:19:53,378
Hey, do you guys want me
to take a family picture?

440
00:19:53,474 --> 00:19:55,059
After all,
I was class historian.

441
00:19:55,172 --> 00:19:57,309
I'm thinking about running
again in middle school.

442
00:19:57,430 --> 00:19:59,234
Actually, uh, could we get
a picture first

443
00:19:59,327 --> 00:20:00,716
of just me and mom?

444
00:20:01,558 --> 00:20:02,773
Really?

445
00:20:04,358 --> 00:20:06,600
Oh. Okay.

446
00:20:13,608 --> 00:20:18,562
Whoo! All right! Let's get
this <i>party-started,</i> huh?

447
00:20:18,677 --> 00:20:19,537
Ha ha!

448
00:20:19,644 --> 00:20:22,002
Actually, we decided to take
the money we would have spent

449
00:20:22,109 --> 00:20:25,185
on a party and get you something
you really wanted.

450
00:20:25,675 --> 00:20:26,842
Happy graduation.

451
00:20:26,964 --> 00:20:29,053
Oh, my God!

452
00:20:29,145 --> 00:20:30,469
It's got an engine
and everything?

453
00:20:30,582 --> 00:20:31,765
For 200 bucks, it better.

454
00:20:31,868 --> 00:20:34,078
Oh!

455
00:20:34,317 --> 00:20:35,354
Ohh!

456
00:20:35,766 --> 00:20:38,275
Wait. So wait.
Seriously, there's no party?

457
00:20:38,368 --> 00:20:39,200
Nope.

458
00:20:39,304 --> 00:20:41,476
So... can I go hang out
with my friends?

459
00:20:43,790 --> 00:20:45,025
Go.

460
00:20:45,203 --> 00:20:47,602
This day just keeps getting
more awesome. Ha ha ha!

461
00:20:47,701 --> 00:20:50,060
I love you guys! Ha ha!

462
00:20:53,351 --> 00:20:55,785
Mom, since there's
no party, would it be okay

463
00:20:55,871 --> 00:20:58,224
if I went over to Carly's
and showed her my license?

464
00:20:58,341 --> 00:21:01,420
<i>Please?</i> I have been waiting
for this day for so long.

465
00:21:01,970 --> 00:21:03,993
Sure.

466
00:21:04,098 --> 00:21:06,585
Aah!

467
00:21:12,481 --> 00:21:13,980
Never leave me.

468
00:21:14,069 --> 00:21:16,984
Don't worry. I won't.
Worry.

469
00:21:17,076 --> 00:21:17,924
Whoop!

470
00:21:18,017 --> 00:21:20,350
<i>Yep, all the work that goes</i>
<i>into raising a kid--</i>

471
00:21:20,442 --> 00:21:23,424
<i>the heartache, the laughter,</i>
<i>the worry, the tears--</i>

472
00:21:23,570 --> 00:21:26,324
<i>it really does go by</i>
<i>in the blink of an eye.</i>

473
00:21:26,628 --> 00:21:28,252
<i>And all those</i>
<i>annoying little things</i>

474
00:21:28,369 --> 00:21:30,170
<i>that seemed so important--</i>

475
00:21:30,332 --> 00:21:32,310
<i>who even remembers</i>
<i>what they were?</i>

476
00:21:40,566 --> 00:21:45,543
Sync and corrections by n17t01
www.addic7ed.com


